CHAPTER.VERS:
And he answered, I haven't troubled Israel; but you, and your father's house, in that you

          {+}
         have forsaken the commandments of Yahweh, and you have followed the Baalim.

And Elijah came near to all the people, and said, How long do you

          {+}
         go limping between the two sides? If Yahweh is God, follow him; but if Baal, then follow him. And the people answered him not a word.

And you

          {+}
         call on the name of your

          {+}
         god, and I will call on the name of Yahweh; and the God who answers by fire, let him be God. And all the people answered and said, It is well spoken.

And Elijah said to the prophets of Baal, Choose

          {+}
         one bull for yourselves, and dress it first; for you

          {+}
         are many; and call on the name of your

          {+}
         god, but put no fire under.
